artup.\n\n\n\nThe configuration issue involves provider-specific parameters: ChatGPT uses a batch size of 50 and standard headers, while Google AI Studio (Gemini) requires a batch size of 75 and custom headers. The `coordinator.py` was sending a unified configuration, leading to the failure.\n\nSuccessfully implemented provider-aware configurations within `src` and `dist_production`, restoring ChatGPT to its base settings and customizing Gemini's. Enhanced Python environment handling ensures the correct `venv` is always used, preventing startup errors. Implemented auto-start and health checks for the server upon provider switching.\n\n\n"}
